BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:To Hold a Mountain
DTSTART:20260508T193000Z
DTEND:20260508T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T193000Z
UID:pCtZg9CKrt
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 105 mins (1h45m)\n\nSemi-nomadic shepherd and cheese
 maker Gara raises her 13-year-old niece Nada as her own. As she fights to 
 protect her grazing land from a NATO military expansion\, Nada begins to i
 magine her own future. This film is generously sponsored by Mary Rainwater
 .\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/to-hold-a-mountain\n\nEstimated start: 
 12:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Renoir
DTSTART:20260508T220000Z
DTEND:20260509T001500Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T220000Z
UID:diDYt0iwNb
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 118 mins (1h58m)\n\nA coming-of-age story following 
 a tomboyish 11-year-old girl whose intellectual father is dying of cancer 
 and mother at her wits’ end. The courageous girl seeks adventures\, some
  involving the paranormal.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/renoir\n\nEsti
 mated start: 15:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Birds of War
DTSTART:20260509T010000Z
DTEND:20260509T024000Z
DTSTAMP:20260509T010000Z
UID:m1pFCiIZxO
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 85 mins (1h25m)\n\nLebanese journalist Janay Boulos 
 and Syrian activist and cameraman Abd Alkader Habak share their extraordin
 ary love story\, told through 13 years of personal archives spanning revol
 utions\, war\, and exile. Director Janay Boulos scheduled to attend.\n\nht
 tps://www.siff.net/festival/birds-of-war\n\nEstimated start: 18:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Friend’s House is Here
DTSTART:20260509T033000Z
DTEND:20260509T052000Z
DTSTAMP:20260509T033000Z
UID:YxwI6UKFSs
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 95 mins (1h35m)\n\nPari and Hanna are best friends a
 nd active participants in Tehran’s vibrant underground arts scene. But t
 he risk of running afoul of the government is omnipresent\, forcing diffic
 ult decisions. This film is generously sponsored by Lynn Dissinger.\n\nhtt
 ps://www.siff.net/festival/the-friends-house-is-here\n\nEstimated start: 2
 0:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Edie Arnold is a Loser
DTSTART:20260509T194500Z
DTEND:20260509T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260509T194500Z
UID:x3O6xfumFu
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 87 mins (1h27m)\n\nLace up your combat boots and whi
 p out that black eyeliner for Edie Arnold is a Loser\, an infectiously cha
 rming coming-of-age flick about a self-proclaimed loser starting a punk ba
 nd at her Catholic high school. Directors Kade Atwood and Megan Rico sched
 uled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/edie-arnold-is-a-loser\n\
 nEstimated start: 13:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:April X
DTSTART:20260509T223000Z
DTEND:20260510T002000Z
DTSTAMP:20260509T223000Z
UID:IOCLX4QZeM
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 93 mins (1h33m)\n\nA black-market body-parts hustler
  (Connor Storrie) desperately searches for his missing twin sister who can
  digitally record her dreams. As he digs deeper\, a sinister conspiracy th
 reatens to consume them both in this sci-fi noir thriller.Producer Lanivia
  Postolache scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/april-x\
 n\nEstimated start: 15:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Under a Million Stars
DTSTART:20260510T011500Z
DTEND:20260510T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20260510T011500Z
UID:fr5oGfZ0au
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 89 mins (1h29m)\n\nExperts and homeless neighbors al
 ike bust myths about Seattle’s homelessness crisis in a deeply reported\
 , humanistic dispatch from the front lines. Recipient of a 2025 SIFF Grant
  for Courageous Documentary Filmmaking. The 2026 Grant Cycle opens May 15 
 on the SIFF website. Director Chezik Tsunoda scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps
 ://www.siff.net/festival/under-a-million-stars\n\nEstimated start: 18:30
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:WTF! Nightmare Fuel
DTSTART:20260510T040000Z
DTEND:20260510T055000Z
DTSTAMP:20260510T040000Z
UID:KET85xsfg2
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 95 mins (1h35m)\n\nFrom the disturbing to the disgus
 ting\, a compendium of short films to haunt your dreams and make you wonde
 r WTF?!\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/wtf-nightmare-fuel\n\nEstimated s
 tart: 21:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
